# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
# Omarchy Mobile storage guard on the Redmi 4 Prime, continued in Arch. The
# initramfs marks the whole eMMC (user area, boot0, boot1) read-only and
# leaves only the microSD card's root partition writable, removing the card's
# whole-disk node. udev would recreate those nodes, so make them inaccessible
# and keep desktop tools away from every Android partition. The card is
# matched by its MMC type, not its number: mmcblk0 and mmcblk1 can swap.
SUBSYSTEM=="block", KERNEL=="mmcblk*", ATTRS{type}=="MMC", MODE="0000", ENV{UDISKS_IGNORE}="1"
SUBSYSTEM=="block", KERNEL=="mmcblk*", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="disk", ATTRS{type}=="SD", MODE="0000", ENV{UDISKS_IGNORE}="1"
